hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7591","7639 Qutaibah told us, he said: Khalaf told us, on the authority of Hafs, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make these supplications: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that is not of benefit, from a heart that is not humble, from a supplication that is not heard, and from a soul that is not satisfied. Then he says: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from These four (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7592","7640 Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Dhubara told us, on the authority of Dhuwayd bin Nafi’, he said: Abu Salih said, Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray: “O God, I seek refuge in You from: discord, hypocrisy, and bad morals.”"
"7593","7641 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Baqiyya informed us, he said: Abu Salamah Sulayman bin Sulaym al-Homsi told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from debt and sin often.” Then it was said to him: O Messenger of God, you often seek refuge from debt and sin. He said: If a man is in debt, he tells a lie and makes a promise. So he left behind.”"
"7594","7642 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Haywa told us, and another mentioned, he said: Salim bin told us. Ghaylan al-Tajibi, that he heard a cyclist, Abu al-Samh, that he heard Abu al-Haytham, saying: He heard Abu Sa`id, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “I seek refuge in God from disbelief and religion.” A man said: O Messenger of God, is religion equated with disbelief? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Yes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7595","7643 Muhammad ibn Bashar informed us, saying: Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to me, saying: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, on the authority of Darraj Ubayy Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “I seek refuge in God from disbelief and religion, A man said: Is religion equated with disbelief? He said: Yes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7596","7644 Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, saying: I am Ibn Wahb. Yahya bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Abd told me. Al-Rahman Al-Hubli, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray with these words: “Oh God I seek refuge in You from: the dominance of debt, the defeat of the enemy, and the gloating of enemies.”"
"7597","7645 Ahmad ibn Harb informed us, saying: Al-Qasim, who is ibn Yazid al-Jarmi, informed us on the authority of Abdul Aziz, saying: Amr informed me. Ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from: worry and sadness.” “And laziness, miserliness, cowardice, burden of debt, and being dominated by men.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7598","7646 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “O God, I seek refuge in You from: the torment of the Fire, the trial of the Fire, the trial of the grave, and the torment of the grave.” And the evil of the temptation of the Antichrist, and the evil of the temptation of wealth, and the evil of the temptation of poverty, O God, wash away my sins with water of ice and hail, and purify “My heart is free from sins just as You cleanse a white garment from filth. O God, I seek refuge in You from: laziness, senility, infatuation, and sin.”"
"7599","7647 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, he said: I heard Mus’ab Ibn Saad, he said: Saad used to teach us these words, and narrate them on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O God, I seek refuge in You from stinginess. I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being sent back to the most miserable life, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of this world and the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7600","7648 Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Musab bin Saad And Amr bin Maymun Al-Awdi said: Saad used to teach his sons these words, just as a servant teaches young men, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He used to seek refuge in them after every prayer: O God, I seek refuge in You from stinginess, I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice. “I seek refuge in You from being sent back to the most miserable life, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of this world and the torment of the grave.”"
"7601","7649 Ahmad bin Fadalah informed us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Omar, “ The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from: cowardice, stinginess, bad life, temptation of the chest, and the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7602","7650 Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rizmah informed us, he said: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr Ibn Maimun, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from five things: from stinginess, cowardice, and bad life.” And the temptation of the chest, and the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7603","7651 Suleiman bin Salim Al-Balkhi informed us, he said: I am Al-Nadr, he said: I am Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, he said: I heard Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from five things: O God, I seek refuge in You from cowardice and stinginess. And the evil of life, and the temptation of the heart, and the torment of the grave.”"
"7604","7652 Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, He said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from: stinginess and cowardice. And the temptation of the chest, and the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7605","7653 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, he said: “ The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge.”, mursal (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7606","7654 Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: I am Ibn Wahb. He said: Salim ibn Ghaylan informed me, on the authority of Darraj Abi al-Samh, on the authority of my father Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from disbelief, And poverty. A man said: And they should be moderate. He said: Yes."
"7607","7655 Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Umm Salamah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him, whenever he left his house, he would say: In the name of God, O God, I seek refuge in You from being humiliated, or from going astray, or from being unjust, or That I am ignorant, or that I am ignored.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7608","7656 Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali informed us, saying: Ishaq bin Issa told us, on the authority of Jarir, and Al-Qasim bin Ma’n, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, On the authority of Umm Salamah, “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, left his house, he would say: O God, I seek refuge in You from being humiliated, or from being humiliated. I will go astray, or I will be wronged, or I will be wronged, or I will be ignorant, or I will be treated ignorantly.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7609","7657 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Umm Salamah, “that Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left his house, he would say: In the name of God, my Lord, I seek refuge in You from being humiliated, led astray, or “I am unjust, or I am wronged, or I am ignorant, or I am being treated ignorantly.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7610","7658 Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told me, he said: Yahya bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu told me Abdul Rahman Al-Hubli, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray with these words: Oh God, I I seek refuge in You from the defeat of debt, the defeat of the enemy, and the gloating of enemies.”"
"7611","7659 Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yahya said: Abu Abdul-Rahman al-Hubli told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray with these words: O God, I seek refuge in You from defeat.” “Debt, and the gloating of enemies.”"
"7612","7660 Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hammad bin Masada told us, on the authority of Harun bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad On the authority of Othman bin Abi Al-Aas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make these supplications: O God, I seek refuge in You from: laziness, “And old age, and cowardice, and disability, and from the trials of life and death.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7613","7661 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, God willing, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from these three: from the depths of misery, the gloating of enemies, bad judgment, and the effort of “The affliction,” Sufyan said: There are three, so I mentioned four, because I do not memorize the one that does not contain it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7614","7662 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to seek refuge from: bad judgment, the gloating of enemies, the enduring misery, and the endurance of calamity. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7615","7663 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from madness, leprosy, leprosy, and other bad diseases.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7616","7664 Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Saeed bin Sulayman told us, he said: Abbad told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from the eye of the jinn and the eye of mankind, so when the two exorcists descended, he took them. And he left everything else.”"
"7617","7665 Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, May God bless him and grant him peace. He sought refuge with these words. He used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from: laziness, senility, cowardice, and miserliness. And evil arrogance, and the temptation of the Antichrist, and the torment of the grave.”"
"7618","7666 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Had, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “O God, I seek refuge in You from: laziness and old age. And the one in love, and the sinner, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of the Antichrist, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7619","7667 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Umair, he said: I heard Musab Ibn Saad, on the authority of his father, said: He used to teach us five things. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would pray for them and say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from Stinginess, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being returned to the most miserable life, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7620","7668 Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Ahmad bin Khalid told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun. He said: I performed Hajj with Omar, and I heard him say in a group: “Indeed, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from five things: O God, I seek refuge in You from Stinginess, cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of life, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of the chest, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7621","7669 Azhar bin Jamil told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sargis, “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, travelled, he would say: O God, I seek refuge in You from the troubles of travel and the depression of a turning point. “And the bitterness after the war, and the supplication of the oppressed, and a bad outlook regarding family and wealth.”"
"7622","7670 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjis, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him, whenever he travelled, he would say: O God, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel, the gloom of a turning point, and the turmoil after a journey. And the supplication of the oppressed, and the bad outlook on family and money.”"
"7623","7671 Yusuf bin Hammad told us, he said: Bishr bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjis, he said: “The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, when he travels, he seeks refuge from: the hardships of travel, the gloom of a turning point, the euphoria after a battle, and the supplication of the oppressed. And bad outlook.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7624","7672 Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali bin Muqaddam informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr. Al-Khathami, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, traveled, he would ride his camel. He said: With his finger and extended Shu`bah with his finger, he said: O God, you are the companion on the journey, and the successor in family and wealth. O God, I seek refuge in You from “And the troubles of travel, and the gloom of a turning point.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7625","7673 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Safwan bin Issa told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ajlan told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id. Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Seek refuge in God from the evildoer in the abode of the shrine, for the evildoer Al-Badi is turned away from you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7626","7674 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Amr bin Abi Amr told us, that he heard Anas bin Malik say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Talha: “Seek for me a boy from among your boys who will serve me.” Then Abu Talha took me out and followed me after him. I used to serve the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whenever he came down, and I often heard him say: I seek refuge in You from anxiety and sadness. And inability and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, burdened by debt, and being dominated by men.”"
"7627","7675 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He used to seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave, and from the temptation of the Antichrist, and he said: “You will be tested in your graves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7628","7676 Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Abraham told me, on the authority of Moses, Abu al-Zinad told me, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I seek refuge in God from the torment of Hell, “I seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in God from the evil of the Antichrist, and I seek refuge in God from the evil of the trials of life and death.”"
"7629","7677 Yahya bin Durst told us, he said: I am Abu Ismail, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, that Abu Salamah told him, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from The torment of the Fire, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of life and death, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of the Antichrist.”"
"7630","7678 Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abu Umar, On the authority of Ubayd bin Khushkash, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: I entered the mosque while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in it, so I came and sat next to him. He said: I entered the mosque, O Abu Dharr, seek refuge in God from the evil of the devils of the jinn and mankind. I said: Do mankind have devils? He said: Yes."
"7631","7679 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told us, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave, seek refuge in God from the trial of life and death, seek refuge in God from the trial of \Antichrist\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7632","7680 Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Ya’la bin Ata told us, he said: I heard Abu Alqamah narrating, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from five things, saying: Seek refuge in God.” From the torment of the grave, from the torment of Hell, from the temptation of life and death, and from the evil of the Antichrist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7633","7681 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, and he mentioned a word that means it. Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata’, he said: I heard Abu Alqamah Al-Hashimi, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God, and is seeking refuge from the torment of the grave, the torment of Hell, the temptation of the living and the dead, and the temptation \Antichrist\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7634","7682 Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata, on the authority of his father, Thus he said: On the authority of Abu Alqamah Al-Ansari, he said: Abu Hurairah narrated to me from in him to in me, he said: And he said, meaning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Seek refuge in God from five things: from the torment of Hell, the torment of the grave, the temptation of life and death, and the temptation of the Antichrist.” This Wrong, the correct one is: Ya’la bin Ata’, on the authority of Abu Alqamah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7635","7683 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He used to teach them this supplication, just as he taught them the surah from the Qur’an. Say: O God, we seek refuge in You from the torment of Hell. I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of the Antichrist, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of life and death.”"
"7636","7684 Muhammad bin Maymun informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, And Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Seek refuge in God Almighty from the punishment of God. By God, from the temptation of life and death, from the torment of the grave, and from the temptation of the Antichrist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7637","7685 Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, I read it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his supplication: O God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of Hell. I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of the Antichrist, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of life and death.”"
"7638","7686 Abu Asim told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Katheer Al-Muqri told us, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar said: He heard Abu Hurairah saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in his supplication: “Oh God, I I seek refuge in You from the temptation of the grave, the temptation of the Antichrist, and the temptation of life and death.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake, and it should be That it is Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Suleiman bin Sinan, and this is not from the hadith of Suleiman bin Yasar, and God is the conciliator and He knows best."
"7639","7687 Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, he said: Abdul Ghaffar bin Dawud told us, he said: Ya’qub bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: “One of the supplications of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was: Oh God, I I seek refuge in You from the disappearance of Your blessing, the change in Your well-being, the suddenness of Your vengeance, and all of Your anger.” Hamza told us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz, he said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukayr told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make supplications, so he mentioned something like it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7640","7688 Muhammad bin Mansour al-Makki informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Seek refuge in God from the punishment of God, seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave, seek refuge in God from the trials of life and death.” “Seek refuge in God from the temptation of the Antichrist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7641","7689 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Badil bin Maysara, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from the torment of Hell and the torment of the grave. And the Antichrist”"
"7642","7690 Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Amr told us, on the authority of Yahya, that he told him, he said: Abu Salamah told me, he said: Abu Hurairah told me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Seek refuge in God from the torment of the Fire. And the torment of the grave, and from the trials of life and death, and from the evil of the Antichrist.”"
"7643","7691 Ahmad bin Hafs told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Jasra, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, Lord of Gabriel, and of measures, and Lord of Israfil.” I seek refuge in You from the heat of the Fire and from the torment of the grave.”"
"7644","7692 Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Sinan Al-Muzani, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: I heard Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in His prayer: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the temptation of the grave, from the temptation of the Antichrist, from the temptation of life and death, and from the heat of Hell.”"
"7645","7693 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever asks God for Paradise three times, Paradise will say: O God, admit him to Paradise.” And whoever seeks protection from the Fire three times, the Fire will say: O God, protect him from the Fire.”"
"7646","7694 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Husayn al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah. On the authority of Bashir ibn Ka’b, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The master of seeking forgiveness is for the servant to say: Oh God You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge my sin to you, and I acknowledge your blessing upon me, so forgive me, for no one forgives sins except you, so if he says it when he becomes certain If he dies, he will enter Paradise, and if he says it in the evening, certain of it, he will enter Paradise.” Al-Walid ibn Tha’labah disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7647","7695 Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, on the authority of Ibn Hab, he said: Musa ibn Shaybah informed me, on the authority of al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abdah ibn Abu Lubaba, that Ibn Yassaf told him that he asked Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “What was the most frequent thing that the Messenger of God prayed for?” Before his death, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: The most frequent supplication he used was: O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, and from evil. \Unless I do\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7648","7696 Imran bin Bakkar told me, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Abdah told us, he said: Ibn Yasaf said: Aisha was asked: “What was the most frequent prayer that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray for?” She said: His most frequent supplication was to say: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, and from the evil of what I have not yet done.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7649","7697 Muhammad ibn Qudamah informed me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Farwa ibn Nawfal, he said: I asked Umm The Believers Aisha: “What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray to?” She said: He used to say: I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, and from the evil of what I have not done. \work\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7650","7698 Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal, on the authority of Aisha She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, and from the evil of what I have not done.”"
"7651","7699 Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: Mu`tamar told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Farwa ibn Nawfal, he said: I asked Aisha, and I said: Tell me about something that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray for. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray. May God bless him and grant him peace, he says: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, and from the evil of what I have not done.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7652","7700 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Husayn, he said: I heard Hilal bin Yasaf, On the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal, he said: I said to Aisha: “Tell me about a supplication that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray.” She said: He used to say “O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, and from the evil of what I have not done.”"
"7653","7701 Muhammad ibn al-Khalil informed us, he said: Marwan, who is the son of Muawiyah, informed us, on the authority of Ali ibn Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Muslim Al-Fazari, on the authority of Jubayr bin Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “Oh God,” and he mentioned the supplication, And he said at the end: “And I seek refuge in You lest he be assassinated from under me.” By that he means: eclipse.” 5 Al-Nasa’i said: Ali bin Abdul Aziz, I do not know him 5. His lineage should go back to his grandfather. Abu Nu’aym disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7654","7702 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, on the authority of Ubadah bin Muslim, he said: Jubayr bin Abi told me Suleiman bin Jubayr bin Mutim, on the authority of Ibn Omar, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “O God, I seek refuge in Your greatness.” That he be assassinated from under me.” In brief, Jubayr said: It is eclipse. Ubadah said: I do not know what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, or what he said. A splint (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7655","Mahmoud bin Sulaiman Al-Balkhi told us, saying: Al-Fadl, meaning Ibn Musa, told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Saifi, Abu’s servant. Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Al-Yusr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from decline and destruction. And drowning, and fire, and I seek refuge in You from Satan tripping me upon death, and I seek refuge in You from dying in Your way, retreating, and I seek refuge in You Because of you I die by stinging.”"
"7656","7704 Yunus bin Abdul-Ala informed us, he said: Anas bin Iyadh informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Saifi, on the authority of Abu Al-Yusr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray and say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from: demolition, decline, and senility. And grief, and drowning, and fire, and I seek refuge in You lest Satan confuse me at the time of death, and lest I be killed in Your cause, retreating, and I seek refuge in You Because of you I die by stinging.”"
"7657","7705 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Abdullah bin Saeed told us, he said: Saifi told me The servant of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Sulami, said thus: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “Oh God, I I seek refuge in You from destruction, I seek refuge in You from deterioration, I seek refuge in You from drowning and burning, and I seek refuge in You lest Satan confuse me when... Death, and I seek refuge in You to die in Your way, retreating, and I seek refuge in You to die by stinging.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7658","7706 Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Al-Alaa bin Hilal told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, On the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, who is the son of Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of Masruq bin Al-Ajja’, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I asked for the Messenger of One night, I was in my bed, but I did not hit him, so I hit my hand on the head of the bed, and my hand fell on the soles of his feet. He was prostrating, saying: I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek refuge in You from You."
"7659","7707 Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, that Muawiyah bin Salih told him, he said: Azhar bin told me Saeed, on the authority of Asim bin Humaid, who said: I asked Aisha: “How did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, initiate the night prayers?” She said: He You asked me about something that no one had ever asked me about. He used to say “Allahu Akbar” ten times, praise “Allaah” ten times, glorify Allah ten times, ask forgiveness ten times, and say: Oh God, forgive me, guide me, provide for me, and keep me safe, and I will seek refuge from the distress of my place on the Day of Resurrection."
"7660","7708 Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Husayn bin Muhammad told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Aisha and Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed in Mecca for ten years while the Qur’an was revealed to him, and in Medina for ten years.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7661","7709 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “There is no prophet among the prophets but that he has been given signs similar to him. Mankind has believed in him, but it was only that to which I was given revelation.” God revealed it to me, so I hope that I will be the most obedient among them on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7662","7710 Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the revelation descends upon him, he will be treated badly for that.”"
"7663","7711 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He asked Al-Harith bin Hisham, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “How does revelation come to you?” He said: Like the ringing of a bell, then it will be separated from me and I have become aware. And it is the most difficult thing for me, and sometimes he comes to me in the form of a young man, and he makes him appear to me.”"
"7664","7712 Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Saif bin Ubaid Allah told us, he said: Sarar told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hattan. Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ubadah Ibn al-Samit, said: “When the revelation was sent down to him, the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was distressed and dismayed. His face, so one day it was revealed to him and he met that. When it was hidden from him, he said: Take it from me. He has made a way for them, the male with the male “And the virgin for the virgin, and the married man for a hundred lashes, then stoning with stones, and the virgin for a hundred lashes, then exile for a year.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7665","7713 Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ata told me, he said: Safwan bin told me. Ya’la bin Umayyah, on the authority of his father, said: “I wish I could see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descending upon him, while we are in Al-Ji’ranah. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a dome, and the revelation came to him. Omar told me to come, so I entered my head into the dome, and a man came to him. He entered ihram in a jubbah for Umrah, anointed with perfume, and he said to the Messenger of God: What do you say about a man who entered ihram in a jubbah when the revelation was sent down to him? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sad about that, so he walked away from him and said: Where is the man who asked me just before? The man was brought, and he said: Either? “The robe, take it off, and as for the perfume, wash it off.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7666","7714 Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la, On the authority of his father, he said: “I wanted to see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he descended upon him. When we were at al-Jiranah, a man came to him wearing Expressions of good manners, and he said: I have declared the ihram for Umrah, and I have to do this, so what should I do? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: How do you do during your Hajj? He said: It was sent down upon him, and he was covered with a garment. Then Omar called me and revealed the garment to me, and I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted, covering his face red."
"7667","7715 Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Ya’qub bin Ibrahim, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Anas bin Malik told me, “God Almighty continued the revelation to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before his death until he passed away.” The greatest revelation occurred on the day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died.”"
"7668","7716 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Ibn Dawud told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Qays, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of Falfla bin Abdullah Al-Jafi said: Abdullah, who is Ibn Masoud, said: “The books were revealed from one chapter, and the Qur’an was revealed from Seven gates based on seven letters.”"
"7669","7717 Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, based on his reading and pronunciation, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me On the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari, he said: I heard Omar ibn al-Khattab saying: I heard Hisham bin Hakim, “He recites Surat Al-Furqan in a different way than I recite it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to me, so I almost I hastened on him, then I gave him time until he left, then I wrapped him in his cloak, and I brought him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: Oh Messenger of God, I heard this man reciting Surat Al-Furqan in a different way than you had read it to me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Read. So he recited the recitation that I heard him reciting, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is how it was revealed. Then he said to me: Recite, so I recited. He said: This is how it was revealed. Indeed, this Qur’an was revealed in seven letters, so read what you can of it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7670","7718 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Yazid bin Harun, he said: I am Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, that Ubayy bin Ka’b said: “He did not confuse It has been on my heart since I converted to Islam, except that I read a verse and a man recited it in a way that I did not read, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to me. Thus, I said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited to me like this, so we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: You recited to me a verse. Such and such, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes, and the man said: You taught me the verse of such and such, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Yes, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Gabriel and Michael, peace be upon them, came to me, so Gabriel went up and sat down. To my right, and Michael sat to my left, and Gabriel said: Recite according to one letter, and Michael said: Increase it, so I said: Increase me, so he increased me. Gabriel said: Recite the Qur’an in two syllables. Michael said: Increase it. I said: Increase it. Gabriel said: Recite the Qur’an in three syllables. He recited the Qur’an in seven letters, so Mikael said, “Add more to it.” He said, “Recite the Qur’an in seven letters. Every understanding person is sufficient.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7671","7719 Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yusuf bin Mahak informed me, he said: I am with Aisha’s mother. The believers, when an Iraqi came to her and said: O Mother of the Believers, show me your Qur’an. She said: Why? He said: I want to compose the Qur’an for him, for we recite it with us without a compilation. She said: Woe to you, and what harm would you have recited before? The first thing that was revealed was a detailed Surah in which there was mention of Paradise and Hell, so that when the people converted to Islam, the lawful and the forbidden were revealed, even if they were revealed. The first thing: Do not drink alcohol. They would have said: We do not stop drinking alcohol. And if the first thing had been revealed: Do not commit adultery, they would have said: We do not stop adultery. And it was revealed: The hour is the worst, and I am passing through Mecca while I am a slave girl playing with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Surah Al-Baqarah and An-Nisa were not revealed except when I With him, he said: So she took out the Qur’an to him and dictated to him the verses of the surahs. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7672","7720 Al-Haytham bin Ayyub informed us, he said: Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Saad, informed us. Ibn Shihab said: Anas bin Malik informed me, “ Hudhayfah came to Othman, and he was fighting against the people of the Levant with the people of Iraq in the conquest of Armenia and Azerbaijan, and he frightened Hudhayfah. Their disagreement about the Qur’an, so he said to Uthman: O Commander of the Faithful, understand this nation before they disagree about the Book, as I disagreed. Jews and Christians, so Othman sent to Hafsa: Send to us the scrolls, so that we may copy them into the Qur’an, then return them to you. So she sent It was brought to him, so he ordered Zayd bin Thabit, Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, Sa’id bin Al-Aas, and Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham: They copy the pages into the Qur’an, and if they disagree with Zayd bin Thabit regarding any part of the Qur’an, then write it in the language of the Quraysh, for the Qur’an was revealed. With their tongue, they did that until when they had transcribed the pages into the Qur’an, Othman returned the pages to Hafsa, and sent to every region a Qur’an of what they had transcribed.”"
"7673","7721 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, who is Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Qur’an was revealed in Ramadan, the Night of Decree, and it was in the lowest heaven, so whenever God wanted to bring about something, it would descend. There were twenty years between its beginning and its end.”"
"7674","7722 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Qur’an was sent down as a whole on the Night of Decree to the lowest heaven, and whenever God wanted to make any of it happen, He made it happen.”"
"7675","7723 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim narrated to us, saying: Al-Faryabi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Saeed. Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Qur’an was separated from the remembrance, and placed in the House of Glory in the lowest heaven, and Gabriel, peace be upon him, made It was revealed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he recited it in a hymn.” Sufyan said: Five verses and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7676","7724 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Asim bin Yusuf told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to have the Qur’an presented to him every Ramadan, so when it was the year in which it was passed, he prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. It was presented to him twice, and he used to seclude himself for the last ten days. Then, in the year in which he was arrested, he secluded himself for twenty days."
"7677","7725 Suleiman bin Dawud informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah Ibn Utbah, that Abdullah Ibn Abbas used to say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the most generous of people, and he was the most generous of people.” Ramadan when Gabriel, peace be upon them, met him, and Gabriel used to meet him every night of Ramadan and study the Qur’an with him. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, when Gabriel meets him, he is more generous than the sent wind.”"
"7678","7726 Nasr bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Mu’tamir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, he said: Ibn Abbas said to us: “i.e. Do you recite the two recitations? We said: Abdullah’s recitation. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the Qur’an once every year. And it was presented to him twice in the year in which he was arrested, and Abdullah witnessed what had been abrogated.”"
"7679","7727 Al-Haytham bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Saad, narrated to me, he said: Ibn Shihab told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Sabbaq, on the authority of Zayd. Ibn Thabit, he said: Abu Bakr sent me the report of the people of Al-Yamamah, so I went to him while Omar was with him, and he said: Omar came to me, and he said: “Indeed Murder was made lawful on the Day of Al-Yamamah by the reciters of the Qur’an, and I think that you should command the gathering of the Qur’an. So I said: How can I do something that the Messenger of God has not done? May God’s prayers and peace be upon him? Then Omar said: By God, it is good. He continued to consult me until God explained my heart to the one to whom he explained Omar’s heart. Then he said: You are a young, sensible boy, and we do not accuse you. You were writing down the revelations to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so you followed the Qur’an and compiled it, so I said: How can you do something that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not do? Abu Bakr said: By God, it is good. He continued to check with me until God explained. My heart goes out to the one to whom he explained the heart of Abu Bakr and Omar. By God, if they had charged me with moving one of the mountains, it would not have been heavier on me than the one who charged me. Then I traced the Qur’an, collecting it all from the sticks, the pieces of paper, the scrolls, and the chests of men.”"
"7680","7728 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, he said: I heard Ibrahim talking, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud was mentioned to Abdullah bin Amr, and he said: “That is a man whom I still love after I heard the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “Recite from four: Abdullah, and Salem, the client of Abu Hudhayfah.” Shu’bah said: He started with these two. Ubayy ibn Ka’b and Muadh ibn Jabal said: I do not know which of them he started with."
"7681","7729 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am a slave, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “I have read to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited seventy-two surahs, and the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, knew that I teach them the Book of God. If I knew that someone knew about it more than me, I would have gone to him. Shaqiq said: So I sat in the circle of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and what I heard someone criticizing that and not returning it.”"
"7682","7730 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub informed us, saying: Suleiman bin Amir told us, saying: I heard Al-Rabi’ bin Anas, saying: “I recited the Qur’an to Abu Al-Aliyah, and Abu Al-Aliyah recited to Ubayy. He said: And my father said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: I was commanded to read to you. The Qur’an. He said: I said: Or was I mentioned there? He said: Yes. Then my father cried. He said: I do not know whether out of longing or fear. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7683","7731 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to my father: “Indeed, my Lord has commanded me to show you the Qur’an.” He said: “Did He name me for you?” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes. Then my father cried.”"
"7684","7732 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdullah bin Idris told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: We told us Yahya, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, said: “The Qur’an was compiled during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, by four people, all of them. Muhammad said: From the Ansar: Ubayy bin Ka’b, Muadh bin Jabal, Zayd, and Abu Zayd. I said: Who is Abu Zayd? He said: One of my paternal uncles? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7685","7733 Bishr bin Khalid told us, he said: I am Gandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite the Qur’an from four: from Abdullah bin Masoud, and Salem The client of Abu Hudhayfah, Muadh bin Jabal, and Ubayy bin Ka’b.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7686","7734 Al-Haytham bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: Ibn Shihab told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Subaq, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, he said: Abu Bakr sent me the killing of the people of Al-Yamamah, so I came to him while Omar was with him, and he said: “The killing took place on the day of Al-Yamama with the reciters of the Qur’an,” and the length of the hadith, repeated"
"7687","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Yazid, he said: It was mentioned to me, on the authority of Abu Masoud, so I met him as he was circumambulating the Kaaba, so I asked him, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat Al-Baqarah in one night, that is sufficient for him.”"
"7688","Bishr bin Khalid told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Jafar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid. On the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Masoud, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites the last two verses of Al-Baqarah in one night, that is enough for him.” Abdul Rahman said: I met Abu Masoud, and he told me about him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7689","Ali bin Khashram informed us, saying: I am Isa, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Masoud. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The last two verses are from the end of Surat Al-Baqarah. Whoever recites them in one night is sufficient for him.”"
"7690","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man reciting in the mosque at night, and he said: Such-and-such has reminded me of a verse that I had omitted. From Surah such-and-such.”"
"7691","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Awf told us, he said: Yazid Al-Farisi told us, he said: Ibn Abbas told us: I said To Uthman ibn Affan: What motivated you to go to al-anfal, which is one of the doubles, and to bara’ah, which is one of the two, and you joined them together? And you did not write the line: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, and you put it in the seven long letters, so what motivated you to do that? Othman said: “When something was revealed to him, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would call someone to write to him and say: Put This is in the surah in which such-and-such is mentioned, and the verses were revealed to him, so he says: Put these verses in the surah in which such-and-such is mentioned. Likewise, Al-Anfal was one of the first to be revealed, and Bara’ah was one of the last of the Qur’an, and its story was similar to its story, and the Messenger of God was arrested. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not make it clear to us that it was one of them, so I thought it was one of them, so I compared them between them, and did not write between them. With a line: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7692","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yazid told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, and Al-Fadl bin Abbas told us Ibn Ibrahim, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Zayd bin Aslam told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Muhammad said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not write anything about me other than the Qur’an,” and Muhammad said: Except The Qur’an, so whoever writes anything about me other than the Qur’an, let him erase it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7693","7741 Muhammad bin Mansour informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “There is no prayer for the one who does not recite the Fatihah of the Book.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7694","7742 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, and Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abd. Al-Rahman, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Sa’id bin Al-Mu’alla, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me while I was praying, so he called me and did not I came to him until I prayed, then I came to him, and he said to me: What prevented you from coming to me? I said: I was praying, and he said: Didn’t God Almighty say: O one? Those who believe respond to God and to the Messenger. He said: Shall I not teach you the greatest surah in the Qur’an before I leave the mosque? So he went to leave. So I reminded him, and he said: Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds, these are the Seven Repeated Verses, and the Great Qur’an that I have been given.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7695","7743 Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Karim told us, he said: Ali bin Abdul Hamid al-Ma’ani told us, he said: Sulayman bin al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on his way, and he came down and a man came down beside him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned to him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Shall I not tell you the best of the Qur’an? He said: So he recited to him: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7696","7744 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman, that he heard Abu Al-Sa’ib, the servant of Hisham bin Zahra, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite the Mother of the Qur’an, It is prematurity, it is prematurity, it is prematurity.” Incomplete."
"7697","So I said: O Abu Hurairah, sometimes I am behind the imam, so he touched my arm and said: Recite it, O Persian, to yourself, for I I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God Almighty said: I divided the prayer between Me and My servant into two halves, so half of it is mine. And half of it is for My servant, and My servant is entitled to whatever he asks. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Recite. The servant says: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. God says: My servant praised Me. He says: The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. God says: My servant praised Me. The servant says: Master of the Day of Judgment. God says: My servant glorified Me, and this verse is between Me and My servant, and My servant has what he asks. The servant says: Guide us to the straight path {6} The path of those You have bestowed upon them neither those with wrath upon them nor those who have gone astray. {7} So these are for My servant, and for My servant is what he asks.” Sufyan bin Uyaynah disagreed with him."
"7698","7745 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sufyan, and he is Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman bin Yaqoub, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Every prayer in which the Mother of the Qur’an is not recited is a prematurity. It is prematurity, it is prematurity.”"
"7699","He said: O Abu Hurairah, sometimes I am behind the imam. He said: O Persian, recite it to yourself, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “God Almighty said: I divided the prayer between Me and My servant, and My servant is entitled to whatever he asked. The servant said: Praise be to God, Lord.” of the worlds, God said: My servant praised me, then when he said: Most Gracious, Most Merciful. God said: My servant praised me, then when he said: Master of the Day Religion. God said: My servant glorified Me, or said: My servant has delegated to Me. So when he said: You are we to worship and to You we seek help, he said: This is between me. And between My servant, and for My servant whatever he asks.” Sufyan said: I entered Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Rahman in his house while he was sick, and I asked him about this. The hadith, so tell me about it"
"7700","7746 Amr bin Mansour told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Al-Rabi’ told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Issa, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: While Gabriel, peace be upon him, was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he heard a voice The opposite of the one above it, and he said: This is a door from heaven that was opened today. It has never been opened before today, and an angel descended from it. He said: This is an angel who descended. To the earth, he has never descended except today, then he saluted and said: Give good tidings of two lights that you have been given that were not given to a prophet before you: the Opener of the Book, And the endings of Surat Al-Baqarah, not a letter of it was recited without being given it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7701","7747 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Do not make your homes graves, for Satan flees from the house in which Surat Al-Baqarah is recited.”"
"7702","7748 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: I am Al-Layth, he said: I am Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Usama, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khabab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of Usayd bin Hudayr, “He was one of The person with the best reciting the Qur’an said: Tonight I recited Surat Al-Baqarah, and my horse is tied, and my son Yahya is lying close to me. He is a boy, so she walked around, so I got up, I have no concern for anyone but my son Yahya, so the mare calmed down, then I read, so the mare walked around, so I got up, I have no concern They are all except my son. Then I read, and the horse galloped and I raised my head, and behold, there was something like an umbrella in the shape of lights, coming from the sky. So he confused me, so I calmed down, and when the morning came, I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him, and he said: Read, O Abu Yahya. I said I have read, O Messenger of God. The horse galloped, and I have no concern for anyone but my son. He said: Read to me, Ibn Hudayr. He said: I have read and I raised my head. Then, behold, it looked like a canopy with lights in it. He astonished me and said: These are the angels, they have come close to your voice. If I had read until morning, it would have been People look up to them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7703","7749 Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Shuaib bin Harb told us, he said: Ismail bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, “He was collecting dates for charity, and he found the print of a palm as if it had been taken from it, so he mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he said: Do you want to take it? Say: Glory be to Him who has subjugated you to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Hurairah said: So I said: Then, behold, a genie. It stood in my hands, so I took it to take it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I only took it for a poor family of the jinn, and it will not I will return. He said: So he returned, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do you want to take it? I said: Yes, so he said: Say Glory be to Him. He made you subject to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: So I am with him and I wanted to take him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he made a covenant with me. That he would not come back, so I left him. Then he came back, and I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do you want to take him? I said: Yes, and he said: Say Glory be to Him who has subjected you to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I said: And behold, I am with him. I said: You promised me, but you lied and returned. I will take you to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Leave me alone. I will teach you some words that, if you say them, no male or female of the jinn will approach you. I said: And what These are the words? He said: The verse of the Throne, recite it every morning and evening. Abu Hurairah said: So I left him and mentioned that to the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said to me: “Did you not know that it was like that?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7704","7750 Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat Al-Baqarah in one night, that is sufficient for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7705","7751 Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, he said: I am Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, and Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat Al-Baqarah, that is enough for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7706","7752 Muhammad bin Mansour informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, he informed him Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat Al-Baqarah in one night, That is enough for him.” Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid said: “I met Abu Masoud during the circumambulation and asked him, and he told me about him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7707","7753 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, On the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with us while Gabriel was with him.” Peace be upon him, when he heard a sound above him, so Gabriel raised his gaze to the sky and said: This door has been opened from the sky that has never been opened before. He said: Then an angel descended, and he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Give good tidings of two lights that you have been given that were not given to a prophet before you: the Opener of the Book, And the endings of Surat Al-Baqarah, you will not recite a letter of it without being given it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7708","7754 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, he said: Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We were preferred over the people by three things: The entire earth was made for us.” a mosque, and its soil was made pure for us, and our rows were made like the rows of angels, and these verses were given, the last of Surat Al-Baqarah from “A treasure under the throne, of which no one was given before me, and no one will be given of it after me.”"
"7709","7755 Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Murrah, he said: Abdullah said: “Khawitim Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed from a treasure beneath the Throne.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7710","7756 Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, and Al-Walid bin Muslim, narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Yahya bin Jabir Al-Tai, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Nawwas Bin Samaan, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the Antichrist. He said: Whoever of you sees him, let him recite the openings of Surat Al-Kahf.”"
"7711","7757 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salem bin Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Maadan, on the authority of Abu Darda, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites ten verses from the Cave will be protected from the temptation of the Antichrist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7712","7758 Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: Baqiyya bin Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khaled bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Bilal, on the authority of Al-Irbad Ibn Sariyah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the Rosary before he lay down, and he would say: “Indeed “In them is a verse better than a thousand verses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7713","7759 Ubayd Allah bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim told me, he said: I am Abdullah, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Ayyash bin Abbas al-Qatbani told me. On the authority of Issa bin Hilal Al-Sadfi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, he said: “A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Recite to me, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Recite three of the same verses. The man said: My years have grown and my heart has become severe. My heart, and my tongue became harsh, he said: Recite three of Dhaat (Ham), and he said the same as his first statement, he said: Recite three of the Rosaries, and he said like His statement, then the man said: But recite to me a comprehensive Surah. He said: Then recite: When the Earth is shaken until he finished it, so he said The man: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never add anything to it. Then the man turned away, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Al-Ruwaijil succeeded. \The Ruwaijal succeeded\"""""
"7714","7760 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Muhajir Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. He said: “I was walking with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he heard a man reciting: ‘Say, O you disbelievers’ until he concluded it and said: ‘He has been acquitted. This is polytheism. Then we walked on, and he heard another person reciting: “Say, ‘He is Allah, One.’” So he said: “As for this man, he has been forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7715","7761 Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahm told us, he said: Ismail bin Jafar told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, Then he mentioned a word that meant it, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Sa’sa’a, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, he said: Qatada bin Al-Numan told me, he said: “A man got up during the night and recited: Say, He is God, One. The surah he repeats, no. He added to it, and when we woke up, a man said: O Messenger of God, a man got up last night after dawn and recited: Say: He is God, One. No more. On it, as if a man was moving it around, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it is equivalent to a third of the Qur’an. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7716","7762 Yusuf bin Issa informed us, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Musa, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Verses have been revealed to me, the likes of which have never been seen: the two exorcists.”"
"7717","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Budil bin Maysarah told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has people from His creation.” They said: Who are they, O Messenger of God? He said: People. The Qur’an, they are the people of God and His special ones.”"
"7718","Muhammad bin Uthman told us, he said: Bahz told us, meaning Ibn Asad, he said: Sulayman bin al-Mughirah told us, he said: Humaid bin Hilal told us, he said: Nasr told us. Ibn Asim, he said: “I came to Al-Yashkuri with a group of Banu Layth, and he said: Who are the people? We said: Banu Layth, so we asked him and he asked us, then we said: We came to you to ask you about the hadith of Hudhayfah. He said: We came with Abu Musa in a group, and the animals were encroaching upon Kufa, so I and a companion of mine sought permission. Abu Musa gave us permission and we approached Kufa. I said to my friend: I am entering the mosque. When the market starts, I will go out to meet you. He said: So I entered. The mosque, and suddenly there was a group listening to a man’s conversation, so I stood up to them, and a man came and stood next to me, so I said to him: Who is this? He said: Are you visual? I said: Yes. He said: I knew that if you were a Kufi, you would not have asked about this. This is Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, so I approached. From him, I heard him say: People used to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about good, and I would ask him about evil, and I knew that good would not come. He precedes me. I said: O Messenger of God, after this good is there evil? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of God and follow what is in it. Three times, I said: O Messenger of God, can there be evil after this good? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of God and follow what it contains three times. I said: O Messenger of God, Will this good be far away from evil? He said: A truce over a smoke, and a group over fighting in it. I said: O Messenger of God, this good will be far away from evil. He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of God and follow what it contains three times. I said: O Messenger of God, is this good more evil? He said: A trial She is blind and deaf, and she has callers at the gates of Hell, and for you to die, O Hudhayfah, while you are stubbornly fighting, is better for you than to follow any of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7719","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Saeed bin Amir told us, on the authority of Salih bin Rustum, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Qart He said: We entered the Kufa Mosque, and suddenly there was a group and a man among them was speaking to them. He said: The people were asking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. About good, and I used to ask him about evil, so that I would know it and fear it, and I knew that good would not escape me. I said: O Messenger of God, is he still Good from evil? He said: O Hudhayfah: Learn the Book of God, and act according to what is in it. So I repeated the statement to him three times, and he said the third time: Sedition and disagreement. I said: O Messenger of God, is there any good after that evil? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of God, and act upon what is in it three times. Then he said on the third: A truce on smoke, and a group on the dirt in it. I said: O Messenger of God, will there be evil after that good? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of God, and act upon what is in it three times. Then he said about the third time: At its doors will be temptations, callers to Hell. It is better for you to die while you are a party to Islam than to follow one of them.”"
"7720","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria told us, he said: Zaid bin Hubab told us, he said: Musa bin Ali told us, he said: I heard my father, saying: I heard Uqba bin Amir, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Learn the Qur’an, sing with it, and acquire it. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it is more escaping.” “from labor in the mind.”"
"7721","Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri, who said: Qubath ibn Razin Abu Hashim al-Lakhmi, from the people of Egypt, he said: I heard Ali bin Rabah Al-Lakhmi, saying: I heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, saying: “We were sitting in the mosque, reading... The Qur’an, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon us and greeted us, and we returned our greetings. He said: Learn the Book of God and acquire it, by the same person as Muhammad. With his hand, he is more escaping in the mind than the tax collector.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7722","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, he said: Alqamah ibn Marthad informed me, he said: I heard Saad ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The best of you is the one who has taught and taught the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7723","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, and Sufyan told us, Alqamah bin Marthad told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah. On the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Shu’bah said: The best of you is the one who learns the Qur’an and teaches it, and he said Sufyan: “The best of you is the one who learned the Qur’an and taught it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7724","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Uthman, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The best of you is he who taught the Qur’an and then taught it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7725","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “It is evil for anyone to say: I forgot a verse. Remember the Qur’an, for it is quicker in detail than the beginnings of “Men are among the blessings of his mind.” Jarir stopped him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7726","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Remember the Qur’an. He is more detailed than men in terms of blessings from his mind, and none of you should say: I forgot a verse, and I forgot. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Rather, he forgot.”"
"7727","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For example The owner of the Qur’an is like the owner of hampered camels. When he treats them, he holds them, and when they are released, they go away.”"
"7728","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Mansour, and Mahmoud bin Ghailan told us, he said: Abu Naim told us, And Muawiyah, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “How wretched” For one of them to say: I forgot the verse of Kit and Kit, but rather he forgot.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7729","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “The example of the Qur’an is only like that of a hamstred camel. If its owner makes a covenant with its mind, he will keep it, and if it neglects it, It went away, when the one who recited the Qur’an stood up and recited it day and night, he remembered it, and if he did not recite it, he forgot it.”"
"7730","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hammam bin Munabbih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If one of you gets up during the night and the Qur’an becomes foreign to his tongue, and he does not know what he is saying, let him lie down\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7731","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, and Imran bin Musa informed us, saying: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’. He said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And peace be upon him. Qutaibah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who is skilled in the Qur’an is with the honorable and righteous traveler, and the one who enjoys it.” He has two rewards,” Imran said: two. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7732","Harun bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ibn Awfa, on the authority of Ibn Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The one who is skilled in the Qur’an is with the honorable and righteous scholars, and the one who recites it while enjoying it.” And it is hard for him, for him there are two rewards.”"
"7733","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad Ibn Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The parable of one who recites the Qur’an and is skilled at it is with the honorable travellers.” The righteous, and whoever recites it while it is difficult for him, will have two rewards.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7734","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “God did not permit anything. He means His permission to a prophet who sings of the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7735","Muhammad bin Hatim informed us, he said: I am Habban, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Qubath bin Razin, on the authority of Ali bin Rabah, on the authority of Uqba, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Learn the Book of God, adhere to it, and sing of it. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, it is more severe.” “to escape from labor in the mind.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7736","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Al-Amash, and another mentioned, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja. On the authority of Al-Baraa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”"
"7737","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: He heard the voice of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari as he was reading. He said: Abu Musa was given some of the psalms of the family of David. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7738","Abu Salih al-Makki told us, he said: Ibn Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God has not authorized anything unless He has authorized a prophet with a beautiful voice with the Qur’an.” \He speaks it out loud\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7739","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has not permitted anything. He has not permitted a prophet to sing the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7740","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Abu Iyas told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Mughaffal, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on his camel and he recited. Then Abu Iyas returned to his reading, and he mentioned on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Peace be upon him: He returned to his reading. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7741","7787 Abdullah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Iyas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Surat Al-Fath on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and I have never heard a better recitation than it. He will return.”"
"7742","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdul Rahman informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It will be said to the one who recited the Qur’an: Read, ascend, and recite as you used to recite in this world, for your status is At the last verse you recite.”"
"7743","7789 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ya’la bin Malik, because he asked Umm Salamah, “about the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his prayers.” She said, “What do you have to do with his prayers?” Then she described He has his own recitation, so if it is described as a recitation that is explained letter by letter.”"
"7744","Taliq ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah informed us, he said: Malik ibn Mughul informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Abu Musa one night while he was reciting, and he said: He was given some of the Psalms of the family of David. So when the morning They mentioned that to him, and he said: If you had told me, I would have written that down in full. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7745","7791 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I asked Anas: “How was it?” The recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: He used to extend his voice."
"7746","7792 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to forbid He travels with the Qur’an to the enemy’s land, fearing that the enemy will attack him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7747","7793 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa’d, “A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. She said: O Messenger of God, I have come to give myself to you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at her and looked upward. He pointed at her, then lowered his head. When the woman saw that he had not performed anything regarding her, she sat down, then a man from his companions stood up and said: That is, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if you do not have a need for her, then marry her to me. He said: Do you have anything? He said: No, by God I found something. He said: Look, even an iron ring. So he went and came back. He said: No, by God, not an iron ring, but this is my garment. He said: Easy: If he has a cloak, she gets half of it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What do you do with your garment, if she wears it, she does not have to wear it? There is some of it, and if you wear it, you do not have to wear any of it. So the man sat until he sat for a long time, then he got up and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him. He greeted a servant, so he gave orders to him and he was summoned. He said: What of the Qur’an do you have? He said: I have Surah such-and-such, Surah such-and-such, Surah such-and-such. He enumerated it. He said: Do you recite them by heart? He said: Yes, and he said: I have made them yours according to what you have of the Qur’an."
"7748","7794 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abu Iyas told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Mughaffal. He said: “I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the conquest, walking on his camel, and he recited: ‘Indeed, We have given you a clear conquest.’” So Abu Iyas returned. In his reading, he mentioned on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “So he went back in his reading (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7749","7795 Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: “ I was walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Uqba, say. I said: What should I say, but he remained silent about me, then he said: O Uqba, Say, I said: What should I say, O Messenger of God? Then he remained silent, so I said: Oh God, return it to me. He said: O Uqba, say, so I said: What should I say? He said: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of Creation. So I recited it until I came to the end of it, then he said: Say, I said: What should I say, O Messenger of God? He said: Say, I seek refuge By the Lord of the people, so I recited it until I came to the end of it, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said at that time: No questioner has ever asked anything like them, nor He sought refuge in something similar to them.”"
"7750","7796 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Yahya bin Hakim Ibn Safwan, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, said: “I collected the Qur’an and recited it every night, and this was conveyed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he said to me: Recite it every month. So I said: Messenger of God, let me enjoy my strength and youth. He said: Recite it every twenty days. I said: Messenger of God, let me enjoy my strength and youth. He said: Recite it every ten days. I said: Messenger of God, let me enjoy it. Of my strength and youth. He said: Recite it every seventh day. I said: Messenger of God, let me enjoy of my strength and youth. But he refused. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7751","7797 Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Sulayman bin Mujalid and Ahmad bin Harb informed us, on the authority of Asbat bin Muhammad, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: I said: “O Messenger of God, how often should I complete the Qur’an?” He said: Complete it in Every month. I said: I am able to do better than that. He said: End it on the twenty-fifth. I said: I am able to do better than that. He said: End it on the twenty-fifth. Fifteen. I said: I am able to do better than that. He said: End it with ten. I said: I am able to do better than that. He said: End it with five. He said: I am capable of doing better than that. He said: He did not permit me. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7752","7798 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I heard Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fast for three days of the month.” He said: “I am able to do more than that.” He said: And he continued until He said: Fast one day, break your fast one day, and he said: Read the Qur’an in a month, so I said: I can endure more than that, until he said: Read the Qur’an. In three \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7753","7799 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He who recites the Qur’an in less than three days will not understand it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7754","7800 Nuh ibn Habib informed us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Muammar informed us, on the authority of Simak ibn al-Fadl, on the authority of Wahb ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “For how long should the Qur’an be read?” He said: In forty, then he said: In a month, then he said : In twenty, then he said: In fifteen, then he said: In ten, then he did not descend, meaning from seven. Wahb from Abdullah did not hear him. Bin Amr (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7755","7801 Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Hassab told us, he said: Muhammad bin Thawr told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Samak bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Wahb bin Munabbih, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, he narrated the hadith of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: “The Prophet commanded him, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: To recite it in forty, then in a month, then in twenty, then in fifteen, then in ten, then in seven. He said: He ended up at seven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
